{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md | sed -n '10,32p;83,115p;127,139p;201,210p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '45,80p;138,185p;199,248p'; rg -n 'D694|D699|D706|D70[789]|part.*whole' docs/DECISIONS.md | tail -18\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md | sed -n '10,32p;83,115p;127,139p;201,210p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '45,80p;138,185p;199,248p'; rg -n 'D694|D699|D706|D70[789]|part.*whole' docs/DECISIONS.md | tail -18\"","aggregated_output":"    10\t## 0. What it decides, and what it can reach\n    11\t\n    12\tIt decides whether linking (poc-v120: Jev's link questions version 2; judging-v8's fuller dependency block) makes the linked number\n    13\tquestions' judgements agree over the release window without harm elsewhere: the evidence for Alex's choice whether the linking version\n    14\treplaces poc-v118 (D699). It is paired on old-2's trajectory (DESIGN.md §1): every request byte-equal to one old-2 sent is answered with\n    15\told-2's answer; only the readers' judgements are bought.\n    16\t\n    17\t**The attainable verdict ($0):** Data Center FY2027 above total revenue FY2027 (`contradictions.py`, calendar dates 07-01..09-20,\n    18\tparser second version, before hand reading): old-1 11 days of 77, old-2 56 of 73, old-3 1 of 33 (that one a misparse,\n    19\t`parser-validation.md`). The class occurs and varies widely between draws; old-2's stored path is an extreme and not a fair control.\n    20\tA linked sequence that reconciles would show near zero; only fresh controls can serve as the baseline.\n    21\t\n    22\t## 1. Arms (paired by draw n = 1, 2, 3)\n    23\t\n    24\t- **linked-n:** poc-v120 from an empty store on its own copy of old-2's archive. Its link jobs are answered only by probe draw n's\n    25\t  answers, matched by request hash (`window_test.probe_answers`; any other link job stops the sequence before a purchase), so its links\n    26\t  are probe draw n's proposals, now written. Readers in all three draws: v9 (Data Center FY2027, reads v14), v14 (total revenue FY2027,\n    27\t  reads v8), v16 (total CPU FY2027, reads v14), v21 (revenue growth FY2027, reads v16, and v9 in draws 2 and 3).\n    28\t- **control-n:** poc-v118 from an empty store on its own copy of old-2's archive, its readers' old judgements retired as below.\n    29\t- **Fresh judgements, delimited by date (round 22):** a reader's link is written by an article of day D_R (v9, v14: 07-10, seq 148;\n    30\t  v16: seq 265's day; v21: seq 534's day); its first affected judgement is its first judgement on a day at or after D_R (old-2: seq 167,\n    31\t  274, 542). Every judgement of a reader on a day at or after D_R must be a fresh answer in both arms: in linked-n because its request\n    32\t  carries the dependency block, in control-n because the old request family is retired. The old family of a reader is identified by\n    83\t**Primary line, P, per pair n (round 24: three outcomes):** over all 73 dates, each arm's dates are definite (D), not definite\n    84\t(overlap or clear, N) or unresolved (U), each date keeping its own arm's class even where the other arm is unresolved. Linked-n's\n    85\tdefinite count lies between D_L and D_L + U_L; control-n's between D_C and D_C + U_C.\n    86\t- **Improved:** D_L + U_L < D_C (the least favourable completion still has fewer definite dates in the linked arm).\n    87\t- **Not improved:** D_L >= D_C + U_C (even the most favourable completion cannot give the linked arm fewer).\n    88\t- **Undecided:** otherwise (the unresolved dates could change the result).\n    89\t- **Testable:** D_C >= 2 (known definite dates of the control over all 73, not only dates readable in both arms).\n    90\t- **Readable:** each arm has at least 60 of the 73 dates resolved **in the hand-read classes** (before any credit adjustment): a\n    91\t  coverage policy that deliberately allows at most 13 unreadable dates per arm (82.2%). A readable forecast with unsupported arithmetic\n    92\t  stays readable; its uncertainty reaches P through the credit-adjusted classes the bounds use.\n    93\t- **Credit (rounds 24–25; one rule):** a **gain** is a date on which the linked arm is not definite and the control is definite. Only\n    94\t  gains are ever adjusted; no other date's class changes for credit. When a pair is provisionally improved, **every** gain is reviewed:\n    95\t  both linked answers in force on it (v9's and v14's), deduplicated by judgement id, are read for July's rule B (arithmetic following\n    96\t  from stated inputs; each assumption that sizes the result disclosed and supported) and for H4. A gain whose forecasts carry a material\n    97\t  rule-B failure on which its reconciliation rests earns no credit (counted definite for P). A gain resting on an unsupported CPU\n    98\t  increment: when the increment can be quantified, the forecast with it removed gives the gain's credit-adjusted class; when it cannot,\n    99\t  the gain counts unresolved: **every** such gain of the pair is marked unresolved, and the bounds are then recomputed once across the\n   100\t  pair (round 26: two gains marked one at a time could each look harmless). Each date keeps its actual class in the report beside its\n   101\t  credit-adjusted class; P is recomputed on the credit-adjusted classes. A confirmed CPU double count stays a harm (H4) whatever its\n   102\t  date.\n   103\t- Reported apart, per arm: definite dates that became overlap and those that became clear.\n   104\t\n   105\t**Harm lines (each checked on all three pairs):**\n   106\t- **H1, refusals (round 24):** on **matched reader-days** (a reader judged on that day in both arms of the pair), the attempted reader\n   107\t  judgements and the model refusals among them (first attempts the code refused, terminal refusals included); refusals on linked-only\n   108\t  propagation days reported apart. Harm at **4 or more** refusals above its control on matched reader-days (3 extra is tolerated).\n   109\t  Rationale, frozen before the run: old-2's stored run refused 4 of 1,616 judgements (0.25%), about 0.6 expected per ~250 reader-days, so\n   110\t  4 extra is far above that base rate while up to 3 stays inside ordinary variation. A **linked double refusal** (the corrected answer\n   111\t  refused again: `judgement_refused_twice` stops the day) is a product failure: the verdict is **fail** whatever else holds; a control\n   112\t  double refusal makes the comparison invalid.\n   113\t- **H2, the fixed trajectory:** an unexplained difference in a non-reader request or its substantive output makes the comparison\n   114\t  **invalid** (not a harm: the paired design no longer holds).\n   115\t- **H3, sourcing through the link (round 23):** a figure an answer presents as the market's (consensus, guidance, an analyst estimate)\n   127\t  named only to say none is supplied). Harm when a linked sequence has a grounding error whose paired control's conclusion in force on\n   128\t  that date does not have the same error type.\n   129\t- **H4, the CPU link:** every post-link v14 answer in the linked sequences is read against the exact CPU conclusion it received and\n   130\t  its control's v14 answer that day. Double counting the CPU forecast is harm. Its effect on P goes only through the credit rule above.\n   131\t- **H5, arithmetic and sourcing (July's rule B):** v9 and v14 at seven fixed dates (07-12, 07-26, 08-09, 08-23, 09-06, 09-13, 09-20) in\n   132\t  all six sequences; the unit is a question-date; Claude reads first, a blind reader second; a disagreement goes to a third,\n   133\t  source-backed read whose class decides. H5 is a separate paired harm count: a linked sequence with at least 2 more material failures\n   134\t  than its control is harm. Its effect on P goes only through the credit rule above (a shared error moves no date).\n   135\t\n   136\t**Verdict precedence:** (1) a **linked double refusal** → fail; (2) **invalid or incomplete** (an infrastructure stop: budget, transport\n   137\tor harness; a control's double refusal; an H2 difference; an arm under 60 resolved dates) → inconclusive; (3) **confirmed harm** (H1, H3,\n   138\tH4 double count, H5) → fail; (4) **untestable** (a control with D_C < 2) → inconclusive, \"the class did not recur\"; (5) **P**: all three\n   139\tpairs improved → pass; any pair not improved → fail; otherwise (some pair undecided) → inconclusive.\n   201\t## 8. Staged send (D708, council round 31)\n   202\t\n   203\tPair 1 (linked-1, control-1) is registered as pair 1 of this comparison and sent first, its two arms together, on the pinned graph and\n   204\tretirement plan; its stores, archives, snapshots and summaries are kept. Its reading (`worksheet.py build-pilot`, `verdict.py --pilot`):\n   205\tthe blind P rows of both arms read by hand and bound to the stores' pairs; H4 on every post-link v14 answer of linked-1; H1 from the\n   206\tdated summaries; the gain review when the pair is provisionally improved. The pilot's decision, by §4's precedence: a linked double\n   207\trefusal fails; an invalid run, coverage short or control-1 under 2 definite dates is inconclusive; an H1 or H4 harm stops; \"improved\"\n   208\tafter the gain review continues to pairs 2 and 3 and the full reading (pair 1's remaining readings done then under the same rule);\n   209\t\"not improved\" or \"undecided\" stops, each with its reason. The pilot never gives the comparison's pass, which needs three pairs. H3's\n   210\tselector and H5's duplicate counting (round 30) are fixed before the full reading, not before the pilot. Pilot cost about $1.96; the\n    45\t    both among the evidence in force.\"\"\"\n    46\t    in_force = store.evidence_in_force(conn, view_id)\n    47\t    recent = store.recent_judgements(conn, view_id, BASIS)\n    48\t    arrivals_after = recent[READINGS - 1]['seq'] if len(recent) >= READINGS else -1\n    49\t    basis = {evidence_id for j in recent for evidence_id in j['cites']}\n    50\t    linked_at = {r['evidence_id']: r['seq'] for r in conn.execute('select evidence_id, seq from evidence_links where view_id=?', (view_id,))}\n    51\t    shown = [p for p in in_force if linked_at.get(p['evidence_id'], -1) > arrivals_after or p['evidence_id'] in basis]\n    52\t    return shown, len(in_force) - len(shown)\n    53\t\n    54\t\n    55\tdef schema_for(prompt_version):\n    56\t    require_supported(prompt_version)\n    57\t    pushes = PUSHES\n    58\t    schema = {\n    59\t        'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False,\n    60\t        'required': ['rung', 'reasons', 'cites', 'cites_views', 'pushes', 'changed', 'why_changed'],\n    61\t        'properties': {\n    62\t            'rung': {'type': 'integer'}, 'reasons': {'type': 'string'},\n    63\t            'cites': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}}, 'cites_views': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}},\n    64\t            'pushes': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': ['evidence_id', 'push'],\n    65\t                                                  'properties': {'evidence_id': {'type': 'string'}, 'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': pushes}}}},\n    66\t            'changed': {'type': 'boolean'}, 'why_changed': {'type': 'string'},\n    67\t        },\n    68\t    }\n    69\t    schema['required'].append('theme_pushes')\n    70\t    schema['properties']['theme_pushes'] = {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': ['view_id', 'push'],\n    71\t                                                                       'properties': {'view_id': {'type': 'string'}, 'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': pushes}}}}\n    72\t    schema['required'][1:1] = STANCE_FIELDS           # after rung: the reference and the implied outcome are written before the reasons\n    73\t    schema['properties'].update({field: {'type': 'string'} for field in STANCE_FIELDS})\n    74\t    return schema\n    75\t\n    76\t\n    77\tdef themes_in_force(conn, view_id):\n    78\t    \"\"\"The theme block of an asset thesis: every open theme thesis with a current state, with its rung label and whether a\n    79\t    changed conclusion was recorded after this thesis's last judgement. Empty for a theme thesis.\"\"\"\n    80\t    if store.view(conn, view_id)['object_kind'] == 'theme':\n   138\tdef _lines_english(conn, view_id, v, rungs, pieces, deps, last, themes=(), hidden=0, full_dependencies=False):\n   139\t    \"\"\"hidden: how many pieces in force are not shown. full_dependencies: the judging-v8 dependency block.\"\"\"\n   140\t    lines = [f'Thesis {view_id} ({v[\"object_id\"]}, {v[\"kind\"]}, focus \"{v[\"looks_at\"]}\", {v[\"year\"] or \"\"}, due {v[\"due_day\"]}): {v[\"question\"]}',\n   141\t             'Ladder: ' + ' / '.join(f'rung {r[\"position\"]} {r[\"label\"]}: {r[\"condition\"]}' for r in rungs), '',\n   142\t             f'[Evidence in view under this thesis, {len(pieces)} items]']\n   143\t    if hidden:\n   144\t        lines.append(f'[Not shown: {hidden} more pieces in force, read in earlier judgements; the previous conclusion carries them]')\n   145\t    for p in pieces:\n   146\t        src = p['sources'][0] if p['sources'] else {}\n   147\t        lines.append(f'- {p[\"evidence_id\"]} [{p[\"tier\"]}; {p[\"speaker\"]}; original source {p[\"original_who\"]} {p[\"original_day\"]}; from {src.get(\"input_id\")} {src.get(\"publication_day\")}] {p[\"one_line\"]}\\n    Quote: {p[\"quote\"][:400]}')\n   148\t        if p.get('replaced'):\n   149\t            lines.append(f'    It replaces {p[\"replaced\"][\"evidence_id\"]} ({p[\"replaced\"][\"original_day\"]}): {p[\"replaced\"][\"one_line\"]}')\n   150\t        if p.get('same_as'):\n   151\t            lines.append(f'    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as {\", \".join(p[\"same_as\"])}; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.')\n   152\t        if p.get('revises'):\n   153\t            lines.append(f'    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of {p[\"revises\"][\"evidence_id\"]} ({p[\"revises\"][\"original_day\"]}); both are in force: {p[\"revises\"][\"one_line\"]}')\n   154\t    if deps:\n   155\t        lines.append('\\n[Current conclusions of the theses it depends on]')\n   156\t        for d in deps:\n   157\t            target = d['resolved_to']\n   158\t            if not target:\n   159\t                lines.append(f'- the {d[\"wait_year\"]} thesis on chain {d[\"wait_chain_view_id\"]}: not yet created ({d[\"direction\"]})')\n   160\t                continue\n   161\t            tv = store.view(conn, target)\n   162\t            state = store.current_state(conn, target)\n   163\t            flag = 'historical only' if d['resolution'] == 'history_only' else ('closed' if not store.is_open(conn, target) else 'open')\n   164\t            rung_label = store.rungs_of(conn, target)[state['rung'] - 1]['label'] if state else 'not judged yet'\n   165\t            if full_dependencies:\n   166\t                lines.extend(_dependency_lines_full(conn, target, d, state, rung_label, tv, flag))\n   167\t                continue\n   168\t            lines.append(f'- {target} ({flag}; {d[\"direction\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"] if state else \"-\"} {rung_label}; reasons: {(state or {}).get(\"reasons\", \"\")[:600]}')\n   169\t    if themes:\n   170\t        lines.append(f'\\n[Themes in force, {len(themes)}]')\n   171\t        for theme in themes:\n   172\t            tv, state = theme['view'], theme['state']\n   173\t            mark = f'; {UPDATED_MARK}' if theme['updated'] else ''\n   174\t            lines.append(f'- {theme[\"view_id\"]} ({tv[\"object_id\"]}, due {tv[\"due_day\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"]} {theme[\"rung_label\"]}; '\n   175\t                         f'judged {state[\"publication_day\"]}{mark}; reasons: {(state[\"reasons\"] or \"\")[:THEME_REASONS_CHARS]}')\n   176\t    if last:\n   177\t        lines.append(f'\\n[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] rung {last[\"rung\"]}; reasons: {last[\"reasons\"][:800]}')\n   178\t    else:\n   179\t        lines.append('\\n[Previous conclusion] none: this is the first judgement, so changed must be true.')\n   180\t    lines.append('\\nAnswer per the JSON schema. cites may name only the evidence ids listed above; '\n   181\t                 + ('cites_views only the dependency thesis ids listed above' if deps else 'cites_views must be empty: this thesis depends on no other thesis')\n   182\t                 + ('; theme_pushes only the theme ids listed above; a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views' if themes else '') + '.')\n   183\t    return lines\n   184\t\n   185\t\n   199\tdef retry_note(errors):\n   200\t    return '\\n\\nThe code returned the previous answer because: ' + '; '.join(errors) + '\\nCorrect it and answer again, citing only the listed ids.'\n   201\t\n   202\t\n   203\tdef themes_shown_in(request_text):\n   204\t    \"\"\"The theme ids of the block a request carried: the ids the answer may name, whatever the ledger says now.\"\"\"\n   205\t    block = request_text.split('\\n[Themes in force, ', 1)\n   206\t    return set(re.findall(r'^- (v\\d+) \\(', block[1].split('\\n\\n[', 1)[0], re.M)) if len(block) == 2 else set()\n   207\t\n   208\t\n   209\tdef evidence_shown_in(request_text):\n   210\t    \"\"\"The evidence ids the request listed: the ids the answer may cite and push.\"\"\"\n   211\t    block = request_text.split('\\n[Evidence in ', 1)\n   212\t    return set(re.findall(r'^- (e\\d+) \\[', block[1].split('\\n\\n[', 1)[0], re.M)) if len(block) == 2 else set()\n   213\t\n   214\t\n   215\tdef check_answer(conn, view_id, data, request_text=None):\n   216\t    \"\"\"request_text: the user message that was sent, so theme and evidence ids are checked against what it carried (a theme may have\n   217\t    closed or opened since); without it, against what the ledger would show now.\"\"\"\n   218\t    errors = []\n   219\t    shown = themes_shown_in(request_text) if request_text is not None else {theme['view_id'] for theme in themes_in_force(conn, view_id)}\n   220\t    named = []\n   221\t    for entry in data.get('theme_pushes', []):\n   222\t        if entry['view_id'] in named:\n   223\t            errors.append(f'{entry[\"view_id\"]} is named twice in theme_pushes')\n   224\t        elif entry['view_id'] not in shown:\n   225\t            errors.append(f'{entry[\"view_id\"]} is not a theme in force shown to {view_id}')\n   226\t        named.append(entry['view_id'])\n   227\t    # the closed set is what the request showed (D198), read from the text that was sent, else computed from the ledger\n   228\t    allowed = evidence_shown_in(request_text) if request_text is not None else {p['evidence_id'] for p in evidence_in_view(conn, view_id)[0]}\n   229\t    not_allowed = lambda e: f'{e} is not among the evidence shown to {view_id}'\n   230\t    bad_push = lambda e: f'push on {e} which was not shown to {view_id}'\n   231\t    deps = {d['resolved_to'] for d in store.dependencies_of(conn, view_id) if d['resolved_to']}\n   232\t    rungs = store.rungs_of(conn, view_id)\n   233\t    if not 1 <= data['rung'] <= len(rungs):\n   234\t        errors.append(f'rung {data[\"rung\"]} outside 1..{len(rungs)}')\n   235\t    for cited in data['cites']:\n   236\t        if cited not in allowed:\n   237\t            errors.append(not_allowed(cited))\n   238\t    for cited in data['cites_views']:\n   239\t        if cited not in deps:\n   240\t            errors.append(f'{cited} is not a dependency of {view_id}')\n   241\t    for push in data['pushes']:\n   242\t        if push['evidence_id'] not in allowed:\n   243\t            errors.append(bad_push(push['evidence_id']))\n   244\t    for field in STANCE_FIELDS:\n   245\t        if not str(data.get(field) or '').strip():\n   246\t            errors.append(f'{field} is empty: state what the market expects and the figure or date the evidence implies')\n   247\t    last = store.current_state(conn, view_id)\n   248\t    if last is None and not data['changed']:\n1038:| D694 | 2026-11-21 | Alex chooses A: a chosen reading link leaves filing alone (D265 applies only to a stated hierarchy); new matching and judging versions open for linking (both opening orders); the July comparison (cap $0.15) after the council passes the $0 proof; the sourced reference not opened | in force | `docs/DECISIONS-log.md` |\n1043:| D699 | 2026-11-21 | Alex continues with A (\"continue\"): the whole-window measurement of poc-v119 against old-2, designed with the council at $0 first; the paid send waits for the council's pass and a ceiling Alex names (~$9 was an estimate) | in force | `docs/DECISIONS-log.md` |\n1046:| D702 | 2026-11-21 | The link census passes its registered gate ($0.0266: known positive 3/3, fragile; no link on the 38 unrelated pairs); beside it, part-to-whole and whole-to-part both occur, one pair flips, and FY2028 growth reads FY2027 CPU with a likely wrong sign in 3/3; council R: probe a sharpened link question at cents before buying judgements, the choice to Alex | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/CENSUS-RESULT.md` |\n1050:| D706 | 2026-11-21 | poc-v120 (matching.link_questions links-v2) passes council review as a product configuration (suite 380, mutants 14/14, the product rebuilds every probe request byte for byte, poc-v119 unchanged); the paid design (round 22) needs four changes before its harness is built | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md` |\n1051:| D707 | 2026-11-21 | Council R passes the paid whole-window design (version 6, rounds 22–27) for building: three linked (poc-v120) and three fresh controls on old-2's trajectory, readers v9/v14/v16/v21, primary line on Data Center above total revenue read by hand with three outcomes per pair, harm lines H1–H5, verdict precedence; harness and dry runs return for review; the send waits for Alex's ceiling | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md` |\n1052:| D708 | 2026-11-21 | Council R (reflection, round 31): a one-pair pilot (linked-1, control-1, about $2) before the full comparison; continue only if pair 1 improves after the gain review with H1 and H4 clear; pair 1 counts in the full comparison; before the send: completed calendar proven, readings bound to the stores, credit defects fixed; ceiling Alex's | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/codex-r31.md` |\n1053:| D709 | 2026-11-21 | Council R passes the pilot of the paid comparison (rounds 32–36; 43 end-to-end checks, the six dry sequences accepted, mutants and stop paths caught): linked-1 and control-1, estimate $1.96, proposed ceiling $2.50; the send waits for Alex's ceiling | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-BUILD.md` |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import json,pathlib,sqlite3,sys,collections,random\nb=pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1]); d=b/'\\\\''linked-1-copy'\\\\''; c=sqlite3.connect((d/'\\\\''views.sqlite'\\\\'').as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\'',uri=True)\nprint('\\\\''copy files'\\\\'', [p.name for p in d.iterdir()])\ns=json.loads((d/'\\\\''summary.json'\\\\'').read_text())\nfor k in ('\\\\''terminal'\\\\'','\\\\''stopped'\\\\'','\\\\''config'\\\\'','\\\\''archive_top'\\\\'','\\\\''acceptance'\\\\'','\\\\''reader days'\\\\'','\\\\''links committed'\\\\'','\\\\''ledger'\\\\'','\\\\''trajectory (H2)'\\\\''):\n print(k,s[k])\nprint('\\\\''calendar'\\\\'',len(s['\\\\''days completed'\\\\'']),s['\\\\''days completed'\\\\''][0],s['\\\\''days completed'\\\\''][-1])\nr=c.execute(\\\"select judgement_id,publication_day,call_id,implied_outcome,reasons from judgements where view_id='\\\\''v14'\\\\'' and publication_day>='\\\\''2026-07-10'\\\\'' order by judgement_id\\\").fetchall()\nprint('\\\\''total'\\\\'',len(r),'\\\\''length'\\\\'',sum(len(x[3] or '\\\\'''\\\\'')+len(x[4] or '\\\\'''\\\\'') for x in r))\n' '/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
