bad theme_pushes set() raw same True deps set() theme-like invalids set() retry []\n9021 Thesis v21 evidence count 31 bad cites set() bad push set() bad cites_views {'v6', 'v5'} bad theme_pushes set() raw same True deps {'v16'} theme-like invalids {'v6', 'v5'} retry [(9022, 'v5 is not a dependency of v21; v6 is not a dependency of v21', False)]\nindependent mask double counts [(7, (153, '2026-07-18', 8766)), (20, (134, '2026-07-16', 8759)), (28, (150, '2026-07-17', 8763)), (54, (118, '2026-07-15', 8756))]\nindependent mask no CPU mentions [(32, (774, '2026-08-23', 8904)), (46, (1363, '2026-09-12', 8989)), (60, (460, '2026-08-08', 8841))]\nmentions of CPU or v8 by field Counter({(False, True): 59, (True, True): 8, (False, False): 3, (True, False): 1})\nmentions in forecast [(67, '2026-07-10'), (69, '2026-07-11'), (118, '2026-07-15'), (134, '2026-07-16'), (150, '2026-07-17'), (153, '2026-07-18'), (174, '2026-07-20'), (705, '2026-08-20'), (748, '2026-08-22')]\nperiod profiles [('v14', ('NVDA', 'How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?', 'total_revenue', '', '2026-02-01', '2027-01-31', 'USD')), ('v16', ('NVDA', 'How much total CPU revenue will NVIDIA generate in FY2027?', 'product_revenue', 'total CPU', '2026-02-01', '2027-01-31', 'USD')), ('v21', ('NVDA', \"How much will NVIDIA's total revenue grow in FY2027?\", 'growth_rate', 'total revenue', '2026-02-01', '2027-01-31', 'percent')), ('v8', ('NVDA', 'How much revenue will NVIDIA generate from stand-alone CPU sales in FY2027?', 'other', 'NVIDIA stand-alone CPU', '2026-02-01', '2027-01-31', 'USD')), ('v9', ('NVDA', 'How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?', 'segment_revenue', 'Data Center', '2026-02-01', '2027-01-31', 'USD'))]\nlinked shared summary {'definite': 3, 'overlap': 1, 'clear': 49, 'ambiguous': 7, 'unparsed': 0, 'dates': 60, 'coverage': 0.883}\nwhole {'definite': 3, 'overlap': 1, 'clear': 61, 'ambiguous': 8, 'unparsed': 0, 'dates': 73, 'coverage': 0.89}\nlink flagged ('2026-07-22', 'definite', (387.3, 387.3, 'year'), (387.0, 387.0, 'year'), 'About $352 billion: v14’s approximately $387.3 billion FY2027 total-revenue forecast multiplied by an estimated 91% Data Center share, between the reported 92% Q1 mix and the around-90% FY2027/FY2028 estimate.', 'Approximately $387 billion for FY2027: Q1 revenue was $81.615 billion and Q2 guidance is $91 billion, an 11.5% sequential increase; extending that sequential growth through Q3 and Q4 gives about $101.5 billion and $113.2 billion, respectively, for roughly $387.3 billion total.')\nlink flagged ('2026-08-03', 'definite', (390.0, 390.0, 'year'), (387.0, 387.0, 'year'), 'Approximately $351 billion: the current dependency forecast of roughly $390 billion total FY2027 revenue multiplied by the third-party estimate that around 90% of FY2027 revenue will come from Data Center.', \"Carrying the Q2 guide of $91 billion, about 11.5% above Q1's $81.6 billion, forward for the remaining quarters gives approximately $101.5 billion in Q3 and $113.2 billion in Q4, or about $387 billion for FY2027. Robust booked demand supports a modest lift, but after discounting orders that span products and periods, the central estimate is roughly $390 billion.\")\nlink flagged ('2026-08-09', 'definite', (415.0, 415.0, 'year'), (386.0, 386.0, 'year'), 'About $374 billion: the current dependency forecast of about $415 billion of total FY2027 revenue multiplied by the roughly 90% Data Center share estimate. The 92% share reported for Q1 would imply about $382 billion if sustained, still below $400 billion.', \"About $415 billion. Carrying the roughly 11% sequential increase in NVIDIA's $91 billion Q2 guide forward gives an operating base near $386 billion for FY2027; customer investment, demand visibility, and some improved supply support a modest uplift, while China exposure and memory constraints temper it.\")\nlink flagged ('2026-08-21', 'overlap', (403.0, 404.0, 'year'), (403.0, 404.0, 'leading'), 'About $371–372 billion: v14’s roughly $403–404 billion FY2027 total-revenue forecast multiplied by NVIDIA’s reported 92% Q1 FY2027 Data Center share. This falls in rung 3 ($350 billion to below $400 billion).', 'About $403–404 billion: $81.6 billion Q1 actual, approximately $94–95 billion Q2, $107–108 billion Q3, and roughly $120 billion Q4 by carrying about 11.5% sequential growth from Q3.')\ncontrol shared summary {'definite': 28, 'overlap': 0, 'clear': 27, 'ambiguous': 5, 'unparsed': 0, 'dates': 60, 'coverage': 0.917}\nchosen control ('2026-07-15', 'definite', (400.0, 400.0, 'year'), (387.0, 387.0, 'year'), \"About $400B for FY2027. FY2026 Data Center revenue of $193.7B carried forward at Q1 FY2027's 92% year-over-year growth implies about $372B; management's Q2 growth-acceleration guidance and stronger demand evidence justify a modest uplift to the rung-2 boundary, while the multi-year, multi-product $1T visibility figure is discounted.\", 'About $387B: carrying the Q1-to-Q2 sequential increase from $81.6B to the $91B Q2 guide forward gives roughly $101.5B in Q3 and $113.2B in Q4, for about $387B across FY2027.')\nchosen control ('2026-08-19', 'definite', (420.0, 425.0, 'year'), (406.0, 406.0, 'leading'), 'Approximately $420–$425 billion for FY2027: starting from the roughly $390 billion consensus reference, a 20% second-half outperformance applied to roughly half of the annual baseline implies about $39 billion of upside before discounting. I discount that uplift for execution and supply constraints and for major commitments whose disclosed timing is after FY2027.', \"About $406 billion: $81.6 billion Q1 actual + $94.5 billion Q2 midpoint of BofA's $94–95 billion expectation + $107.5 billion Q3 midpoint of its $107–108 billion potential guidance estimate + about $122 billion Q4, carrying forward the roughly 13.8% Q2-to-Q3 sequential growth rate.\")\nchosen control ('2026-08-23', 'definite', (436.0, 436.0, 'year'), (407.0, 407.0, 'leading'), 'About $436 billion: estimate Q2 at roughly $84 billion by applying Q1’s approximately 92% Data Center share to the $91 billion total-revenue guide, giving about $159 billion in the first half. Subtracting that from the $390 billion baseline leaves about $231 billion for the second half; SemiAnalysis’s 20% above-estimates view implies about $277 billion there and roughly $436 billion for FY2027.', \"About $407 billion: start with reported Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion, use the $91 billion Q2 guide, take roughly $107.5 billion as a Q3 anchor from BofA's $107–108 billion expected guidance, then carry the roughly 18% Q2-to-Q3 increase into Q4 (about $127 billion).\")\nchosen control ('2026-08-25', 'definite', (438.6, 438.6, 'year'), (402.0, 403.0, 'leading'), 'Approximately $438.6 billion: $75.25 billion of Q1 revenue plus the latest $86.3 billion Q2 estimate gives about $161.6 billion for the first half; carrying forward the prior roughly $277 billion second-half implication from analyst estimates uplifted 20% gives about $438.6 billion for FY2027.', 'About $402–403 billion: reported Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion, Q2 around $94–95 billion and Q3 around $107–108 billion from specific forecasts, then roughly 11% sequential growth into Q4 to about $119 billion.')\nchosen control ('2026-09-06', 'definite', (426.0, 426.0, 'year'), (407.1, 407.1, 'leading'), 'About $426 billion: FY2027 Q1 and Q2 contribute $164.25 billion; the $108 billion Q3 total-revenue outlook at a 92.5% Data Center mix implies about $99.9 billion for Q3. Carrying roughly 18% sequential growth into Q4 gives about $118 billion; that makes an analyst-estimate H2 base near $218 billion, which SemiAnalysis’s 20% H2 outperformance forecast lifts to about $261 billion, or roughly $426 billion for the year.', 'About $407.1 billion: add reported Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion and Q2 revenue of $96.2 billion to Q3 guidance of $108.0 billion, then carry the 12.3% sequential growth embedded in Q3 guidance into Q4, implying about $121.3 billion.')\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"I marked four CPU double counts before restoring the dates and IDs. The matched-day count also reproduces five linked refusals against one control refusal. The archived requests contain two details that change how I’d describe the refusal mechanism and the proposed fix."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt | sed -n '4,11p'; cmp -s src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v8.txt; print -r -- status=\"'$?; rg -n '\"'part.*whole|whole.*part|CPU|guidance|sum|policy|structur' docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/{DESIGN.md,WORDING-V2.md,PROBE-V2-RESULT.md,pinned-plan.json} | head -70; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/paid_run.py | sed -n '158,187p;258,276p;301,319p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt | sed -n '4,11p'; cmp -s src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v8.txt; print -r -- status=\"'$?; rg -n '\"'part.*whole|whole.*part|CPU|guidance|sum|policy|structur' docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/{DESIGN.md,WORDING-V2.md,PROBE-V2-RESULT.md,pinned-plan.json} | head -70; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/paid_run.py | sed -n '158,187p;258,276p;301,319p'\"","aggregated_output":"     4\t- Judge against a reference: what the market expects for this question (consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline). Say where the reference sits on the ladder. A consensus or guidance figure by itself keeps the judgement at the reference's rung; once other evidence has arrived it is never the reason to stay. Then derive the outcome the evidence implies: reported figures and guidance give a run-rate that carries the guided growth forward, never the last quarter annualised flat; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it. A target for a product with no shipments yet is discounted by default; it is taken in full only when the evidence shows the volume in hand. State the implied figure or date, check it against the dependencies' conclusions shown (a part cannot exceed its whole, and a figure that spans several periods or products gives this question only its share), compare it with the rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.\n     5\t- Weigh by tier and by novelty. Only fact can establish that a rung's outcome already holds; \"not established\" is a statement of confidence, never a reason to stay. Guidance for the current or next quarter is the strongest forecast input. A management target for a product not yet shipping, or an ambition spanning years, is an input to be discounted for time and execution (how many selling quarters remain, what volume and price the figure implies, what the company's own choices say), not an answer; consensus is where the market stands, not the answer either. third_party_view and rumour move the forecast in proportion to their specificity (a number, a date, a named party): a research firm's shipment or revenue tracking with a number counts. A commitment or deal that is announced but not sized is sized from its disclosed comparable (the same programme's other deal, scaled by capacity or units); a figure no one states is derived from the accounting identities in the evidence when they allow it. A repeat, another outlet for the same claim, or an opinion that adds no new fact or calculation moves nothing. Missing confirmation alone is not grounds for the lowest or highest rung: an event not being confirmed is not confirmation that it did not happen.\n     6\t- An evidence item that replaces another includes its predecessor for context, such as guidance revised from 12% to 25% growth. The predecessor is no longer evidence in force.\n     7\t- “Themes in force” lists the library's open theme theses (policy stages, shared quantities) with their current conclusions. They are our own judgements, never evidence: do not cite them in cites. Weigh each one that bears on this thesis and report it in theme_pushes with the direction it pushes this thesis (toward_first, toward_last or none); leave out a theme that does not bear on it. A theme marked “updated since this thesis was last judged” may change the conclusion; one that is not marked already stood at the previous judgement. When no themes are listed, theme_pushes is empty.\n     8\t- A dependency marked “not yet created” supplies no input. A dependency marked “historical only” is closed without a successor; its closing conclusion is background only.\n     9\t- Your conclusion must be consistent with the conclusions of the theses it depends on and the themes in force as shown: a share cannot be judged at zero while the policy that gates it is judged likely to open; a component cannot exceed its whole.\n    10\t- Return the rung's one-based position; reference (what the market expects and which rung that is); implied_outcome (the figure or date the evidence implies and how you derived it, in one or two sentences); reasons (the gap between the two and why it does or does not cross a rung boundary); citations to supplied evidence and dependency IDs; each evidence item's push (toward_first, toward_last or none); theme_pushes; changed; and why_changed. Write explanations in English; preserve IDs and any quoted source text.\n    11\t- changed is true for a different rung or a change to the key facts or figures supporting the same rung, including a changed implied outcome. Repetition or another source for the same statement does not alone change the conclusion. The first judgement always has changed true.\nstatus=0\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md:4:unsupported links including the base effect, no blanket ban on a whole reading its part. The probe is harness-only: `window_test.py\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md:11:| Part against whole, direction unsettled: v9–v14 at margins 0.03–0.09; v21–v9 flips between draws; whole-to-part and part-to-whole both occur | READS `candidate_reads_thesis`: \"a part read against its whole (...), or a quantity read against another it depends on (...)\": the second clause lets a whole \"depend on\" its part; no sentence says which reads when both fit | D537: the total carried the year's consensus and guidance that the segment's requests lacked; D260: a judgement is made against what the market expects (consensus, guidance, the stated plan) | **abstract** (two clauses, both directions, no tie-break) |\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md:12:| Across periods with an unsupported sign: v17 (FY2028 growth) reads v16 (FY2027 CPU), together, 3 of 3; v35 (FY2028 total) reads v9 (FY2027 Data Center), 1 of 3 | no READS sentence on periods (`neither` covers only \"the same quantity for the same period and scope\"); every SIGN example is within one period | the arithmetic of a growth rate (a higher base lowers next year's growth at a given level); the dependency design §2: another period of the same quantity \"may be linked\" | **missing** |\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md:17:> When either question could be judged with the other in view, the one whose answer the supplied text anchors less (no guidance,\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md:29:both ways: a part with guidance and a whole without would have the whole read the part. No direction is banned.\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md:33:carrying the year's consensus), and D260 explains why guidance and consensus anchor a judgement (it governs judging, not linking). The\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md:46:whose shown text gives no bridge, the two unsupported links council R named (321:v16, v17 FY2028 growth against v16 FY2027 CPU; 1238:v9,\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md:71:  unchanged in bytes, checksum and requests. `poc/config/poc-v120.json` = poc-v119 with `\"link_questions\": \"links-v2\"`.\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md:82:| State × event | a run keeps one configuration (as for v118/v119, DESIGN.md §0); a store written under poc-v120 and opened under poc-v119 or poc-v118 is read the same (the written rows do not carry the question version; the selection record carries the config checksum); a configuration changed between days is the defined outcome of D694 §0, not a supported mode. |\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PROBE-V2-RESULT.md:18:| v17 (FY2028 growth) reads v16 (FY2027 CPU), together | 3/3 | 0/3 | **removed** (the base-effect risk) |\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PROBE-V2-RESULT.md:21:| v21 (FY2027 growth) reads v16 (FY2027 CPU) | 3/3 | 3/3 | kept |\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PROBE-V2-RESULT.md:22:| v16 (total CPU) reads v14 (total revenue) | 3/3 | 3/3 | kept |\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PROBE-V2-RESULT.md:25:| **v14 (total revenue) reads v8 (stand-alone CPU)** | 0/3 (0.47, 0.46, 0.44: below the line) | **3/3 (0.53, 0.54, 0.58)** | **added**: a whole reading a part about 5% of it; the tie-break points the other way (the total carries the full-year estimate) |\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PROBE-V2-RESULT.md:26:| v16 (total CPU) reads v8 (stand-alone CPU) | 0/3 | 1/3 | added once: a whole reading its part |\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PROBE-V2-RESULT.md:34:  in the direction it should have refused. A whole reading a part a twentieth its size gives the total little; it also makes v14 a\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PROBE-V2-RESULT.md:40:- v14 reads v8 is weak with plausible downstream harm: the total had a direct $393B FY2027 estimate and the CPU card no full-year\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PROBE-V2-RESULT.md:41:  NVIDIA CPU forecast, so the tie-break favoured the CPU question reading the total; the risk is the total treating an uncertain CPU\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PROBE-V2-RESULT.md:48:  which CPU conclusion the linked total saw, how that total compares with its control, and which total Data Center saw; judge Data\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md:56:| 49 | v8 stand-alone CPU revenue FY2027 | 2 |\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md:60:| 265 | v16 total CPU revenue FY2027 | 6 |\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md:74:0.5 or more (`links.THRESHOLD`), so a shift of 0.02 gives no link or the opposite link. The same opening's v14–v8 (stand-alone CPU)\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md:78:**Mechanism (prompt audit, `links.READS_CRITERIA`):** \"candidate_reads_thesis\" covers \"a part read against its whole ... or a\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md:82:**abstract** (the criterion admits both directions for a part against its whole).\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md:104:capacity and may buy back unsold capacity; supply commitments against revenue, margin or the capacity backstops; CPU parts against\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md:105:totals far above them; growth against its amount; another period). Round 14 moved the CPU-to-total and credit-support-to-revenue pairs\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md:121:wording that fixes the part-and-whole direction changes what the system does and goes to Alex with options and a recommendation before\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md:160:Round 13's points, to be taken into this rule before its own round: part–whole contradiction only on matching scope and period, a\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md:163:forecast); July's arithmetic-and-assumption check kept; rates on common question-pair dates, the three whole trajectories as the\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md:170:- **B, contradiction:** for a part read against its whole, R's implied outcome above T's implied outcome, or leaving less for the rest\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md:196:| a process dies | the sequence is final (never resumed); the reservation stays counted |\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md:202:whole window), D537 (part reads whole) and PRD 06 line 134 (D368/D208: root reads drivers), D677 (no paid work unless Alex funds a run\n   158\t        self.snapshots, self.snapshot_problems, self.snapshot_checks = [], [], 0\n   159\t        self.day_windows, self.terminal = {}, None\n   160\t        self.lock = threading.Lock()\n   161\t\n   162\t    def transport(self, *args):\n   163\t        request = args[-1]\n   164\t        if len(args) == 1:\n   165\t            if july_test.is_link_request(request) and self.kind == 'linked':\n   166\t                sha = model.request_identity(request)[1]\n   167\t                if sha not in self.probe:\n   168\t                    raise july_test.Stop(f'a link job outside probe draw {self.draw} ({sha[:12]}): not sent')\n   169\t                self.link_jobs.append(sha)\n   170\t                return self.probe[sha]\n   171\t            raise july_test.Stop('a Jev request missed the archive: not sent')\n   172\t        sha = model.request_identity(request)[1]\n   173\t        view_id = july_test.judged_view(request) if is_judgement_request(request) else None\n   174\t        if view_id is not None and view_id not in self.reader_days:\n   175\t            response = self.stored_refusals.pop(sha, None)\n   176\t            if response is not None:\n   177\t                self.refusals_given.append(sha[:12])\n   178\t                return response\n   179\t        day = self.day\n   180\t        allowed = view_id in self.reader_days and day is not None and day >= self.reader_days[view_id]\n   181\t        text = request['messages'][-1]['content']\n   182\t        with self.lock:\n   183\t            self.attempts.append({'view': view_id, 'day': day, 'sha': sha, 'retry': 'Correct it and answer again' in text, 'admitted': allowed})\n   184\t        if allowed:\n   185\t            self.check_snapshot(view_id, day, text)\n   186\t        return self.latch.run(allowed, f'unapproved request on {day} (thesis {view_id}): not sent', (view_id, day),\n   187\t                              lambda: self.inner(*args))\n   258\tdef prepare(folder, kind, draw):\n   259\t    if folder.exists():\n   260\t        raise SystemExit(f'{folder} exists: a sequence starts from an empty folder and is never resumed')\n   261\t    folder.mkdir(parents=True)\n   262\t    shutil.copyfile(OLD2 / 'archive.sqlite', folder / 'archive.sqlite')\n   263\t    archive = model.Archive(str(folder / 'archive.sqlite'))\n   264\t    top = archive.conn.execute('select coalesce(max(call_id), 0) from model_calls').fetchone()[0]\n   265\t    retired = []\n   266\t    if kind == 'control':\n   267\t        for reader, calls in retired_rows(readers(draw)).items():\n   268\t            for call_id in calls:\n   269\t                archive.retire(call_id)\n   270\t                retired.append((reader, call_id))\n   271\t    views = folder / 'views.sqlite'\n   272\t    marker = sqlite3.connect(views)\n   273\t    marker.execute('create table harness_only (name text, day text)')\n   274\t    marker.execute(\"insert into harness_only values ('paid_run.py', '2026-11-21')\")\n   275\t    marker.commit()\n   276\t    marker.close()\n   301\tdef run_sequence(out, kind, draw, inner, ledger_state, transport_kind):\n   302\t    if kind not in ('linked', 'control') or draw not in DRAWS:\n   303\t        raise SystemExit('kind must be linked or control, draw 1, 2 or 3')\n   304\t    pinned = pinned_plan(draw)\n   305\t    folder = out / f'{kind}-{draw}'\n   306\t    archive, top, retired = prepare(folder, kind, draw)\n   307\t    run = SequenceRun(kind, draw, inner, folder)\n   308\t    cfg = config.load(str(V120 if kind == 'linked' else V118))\n   309\t    summary = {'kind': kind, 'draw': draw, 'transport': transport_kind, 'config': cfg.version, 'archive_top': top,\n   310\t               'reader days': run.reader_days, 'retired rows': len(retired), 'stopped': ''}\n   311\t    original_judge_day, original_build = round_module.judge_day, judging.build_prompt\n   312\t    round_module.judge_day, judging.build_prompt = run.judge_day(original_judge_day), run.build_prompt(original_build)\n   313\t    held = live_lock.acquire(str(folder / 'views.sqlite'))\n   314\t    try:\n   315\t        replay.run(testdb_path=str(ITEMS), views_path=str(folder / 'views.sqlite'), archive=archive, cfg=cfg, universe=universe.load(str(UNIVERSE)),\n   316\t                   from_day=WINDOW[0], until_day=WINDOW[1], transport=run.transport, log=lambda *a: None, only_objects={'NVDA'})\n   317\t    except Exception as error:\n   318\t        summary['stopped'] = f'{type(error).__name__}: {error}'[:500]\n   319\t        if run.terminal is None:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import collections,json,pathlib,re,sqlite3,sys\nsys.path.insert(0,'\\\\''src'\\\\'')\nfrom hivemind.views import judging\nb=pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1]); root=pathlib.Path('\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run'\\\\'')\ndef op(p):\n return sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\'',uri=True)\ndef refs(t,d):\n e=judging.evidence_shown_in(t); th=judging.themes_shown_in(t)\n ds=set(re.findall(r'\\\\''\"'^- (v'\"\\\\d+) \\\\('\\\\'',t.partition('\\\\''\\\\n[Current conclusions of the theses it depends on]'\\\\'')[2].split('\\\\''\\\\n\\\\n['\\\\'',1)[0],re.M))\n return {'\\\\''cites'\\\\'':set(d['\\\\''cites'\\\\''])-e,'\\\\''pushes'\\\\'':{p['\\\\''evidence_id'\\\\''] for p in d['\\\\''pushes'\\\\'']}-e,'\\\\''cites_views'\\\\'':set(d['\\\\''cites_views'\\\\''])-ds,'\\\\''theme_pushes'\\\\'':{p['\\\\''view_id'\\\\''] for p in d['\\\\''theme_pushes'\\\\'']}-th}\npaths=[(n,root/n/'\\\\''prod'\\\\'') for n in ('\\\\''old-1'\\\\'','\\\\''old-2'\\\\'','\\\\''old-3'\\\\'')]+[(n,b/(n+'\\\\''-copy'\\\\'')) for n in ('\\\\''control-1'\\\\'','\\\\''linked-1'\\\\'')]\nfor name,path in paths:\n a,v=op(path/'\\\\''archive.sqlite'\\\\''),op(path/'\\\\''views.sqlite'\\\\'')\n judged={i for i, in v.execute('\\\\''select call_id from judgements'\\\\'')}\n s=json.loads((path/'\\\\''summary.json'\\\\'').read_text()) if name in ('\\\\''control-1'\\\\'','\\\\''linked-1'\\\\'') else None\n ids={r['\\\\''call_id'\\\\''] for r in s['\\\\''archive judge rows written (dated)'\\\\''] if r['\\\\''reader'\\\\'']} if s else None\n result=collections.Counter(); surprises=[]\n for i,sha,request,answer in a.execute(\\\"select call_id,request_sha256,request_json,answer_json from model_calls where purpose='\\\\''judge'\\\\'' order by call_id\\\"):\n  if ids is not None and i not in ids:continue\n  req=json.loads(request)['\\\\''messages'\\\\''][-1]['\\\\''content'\\\\'']; ans=json.loads(answer)\n  bad={k:vv for k,vv in refs(req,ans).items() if vv}\n  state='\\\\''refused'\\\\'' if '\\\\'':refused:'\\\\'' in sha else '\\\\''stored accepted'\\\\'' if i in judged else '\\\\''other archive entry'\\\\''\n  result[(state,bool(bad))]+=1\n  if (state=='\\\\''refused'\\\\'')\"'!=bool(bad):surprises.append((i,state,bad,req.splitlines()[0].split('\"'\\\\'' ('\\\\'')[0]))\n print(name,len(judged),result,'\\\\''surprises'\\\\'',surprises[:10])\n if name=='\\\\''linked-1'\\\\'':\n  for j,day,aid,co in v.execute(\\\"select judgement_id,publication_day,call_id,implied_outcome from judgements where judgement_id in (118,134,150,153,174) order by publication_day\\\"):\n   req=json.loads(a.execute('\\\\''select request_json from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\'',(aid,)).fetchone()[0])['\\\\''messages'\\\\''][-1]['\\\\''content'\\\\'']\n   dependency=req.partition('\\\\''\\\\n[Current conclusions of the theses it depends on]'\\\\'')[2].split('\\\\''\\\\n\\\\n['\\\\'',1)[0].splitlines()[:5]\n   cv=op(b/'\\\\''control-1-copy/views.sqlite'\\\\''); baseline=cv.execute(\\\"select judgement_id,publication_day,implied_outcome from judgements where view_id='\\\\''v14'\\\\'' and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1\\\",(day,)).fetchone()\n   print('\\\\''H4'\\\\'',j,day,dependency[:4],'\\\\''control'\\\\'',baseline)\n  for cid in [8777,8822,8848,8855,8888,8909,9021]:\n   request=json.loads(a.execute('\\\\''select request_json from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\'',(cid,)).fetchone()[0])\n   print('\\\\''closing ids rule'\\\\'',cid,request['\\\\''messages'\\\\''][-1]['\\\\''content'\\\\''].splitlines()[-1])\n' '/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import collections,json,pathlib,re,sqlite3,sys\nsys.path.insert(0,'\\\\''src'\\\\'')\nfrom hivemind.views import judging\nb=pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1]); root=pathlib.Path('\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run'\\\\'')\ndef op(p):\n return sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\'',uri=True)\ndef refs(t,d):\n e=judging.evidence_shown_in(t); th=judging.themes_shown_in(t)\n ds=set(re.findall(r'\\\\''\"'^- (v'\"\\\\d+) \\\\('\\\\'',t.partition('\\\\''\\\\n[Current conclusions of the theses it depends on]'\\\\'')[2].split('\\\\''\\\\n\\\\n['\\\\'',1)[0],re.M))\n return {'\\\\''cites'\\\\'':set(d['\\\\''cites'\\\\''])-e,'\\\\''pushes'\\\\'':{p['\\\\''evidence_id'\\\\''] for p in d['\\\\''pushes'\\\\'']}-e,'\\\\''cites_views'\\\\'':set(d['\\\\''cites_views'\\\\''])-ds,'\\\\''theme_pushes'\\\\'':{p['\\\\''view_id'\\\\''] for p in d['\\\\''theme_pushes'\\\\'']}-th}\npaths=[(n,root/n/'\\\\''prod'\\\\'') for n in ('\\\\''old-1'\\\\'','\\\\''old-2'\\\\'','\\\\''old-3'\\\\'')]+[(n,b/(n+'\\\\''-copy'\\\\'')) for n in ('\\\\''control-1'\\\\'','\\\\''linked-1'\\\\'')]\nfor name,path in paths:\n a,v=op(path/'\\\\''archive.sqlite'\\\\''),op(path/'\\\\''views.sqlite'\\\\'')\n judged={i for i, in v.execute('\\\\''select call_id from judgements'\\\\'')}\n s=json.loads((path/'\\\\''summary.json'\\\\'').read_text()) if name in ('\\\\''control-1'\\\\'','\\\\''linked-1'\\\\'') else None\n ids={r['\\\\''call_id'\\\\''] for r in s['\\\\''archive judge rows written (dated)'\\\\''] if r['\\\\''reader'\\\\'']} if s else None\n result=collections.Counter(); surprises=[]\n for i,sha,request,answer in a.execute(\\\"select call_id,request_sha256,request_json,answer_json from model_calls where purpose='\\\\''judge'\\\\'' order by call_id\\\"):\n  if ids is not None and i not in ids:continue\n  req=json.loads(request)['\\\\''messages'\\\\''][-1]['\\\\''content'\\\\'']; ans=json.loads(answer)\n  bad={k:vv for k,vv in refs(req,ans).items() if vv}\n  state='\\\\''refused'\\\\'' if '\\\\'':refused:'\\\\'' in sha else '\\\\''stored accepted'\\\\'' if i in judged else '\\\\''other archive entry'\\\\''\n  result[(state,bool(bad))]+=1\n  if (state=='\\\\''refused'\\\\'')\"'!=bool(bad):surprises.append((i,state,bad,req.splitlines()[0].split('\"'\\\\'' ('\\\\'')[0]))\n print(name,len(judged),result,'\\\\''surprises'\\\\'',surprises[:10])\n if name=='\\\\''linked-1'\\\\'':\n  for j,day,aid,co in v.execute(\\\"select judgement_id,publication_day,call_id,implied_outcome from judgements where judgement_id in (118,134,150,153,174) order by publication_day\\\"):\n   req=json.loads(a.execute('\\\\''select request_json from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\'',(aid,)).fetchone()[0])['\\\\''messages'\\\\''][-1]['\\\\''content'\\\\'']\n   dependency=req.partition('\\\\''\\\\n[Current conclusions of the theses it depends on]'\\\\'')[2].split('\\\\''\\\\n\\\\n['\\\\'',1)[0].splitlines()[:5]\n   cv=op(b/'\\\\''control-1-copy/views.sqlite'\\\\''); baseline=cv.execute(\\\"select judgement_id,publication_day,implied_outcome from judgements where view_id='\\\\''v14'\\\\'' and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1\\\",(day,)).fetchone()\n   print('\\\\''H4'\\\\'',j,day,dependency[:4],'\\\\''control'\\\\'',baseline)\n  for cid in [8777,8822,8848,8855,8888,8909,9021]:\n   request=json.loads(a.execute('\\\\''select request_json from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\'',(cid,)).fetchone()[0])\n   print('\\\\''closing ids rule'\\\\'',cid,request['\\\\''messages'\\\\''][-1]['\\\\''content'\\\\''].splitlines()[-1])\n' '/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad'\"","aggregated_output":"old-1 1609 Counter({('stored accepted', False): 1609, ('refused', True): 1}) surprises []\nold-2 1616 Counter({('stored accepted', False): 1616, ('refused', True): 4}) surprises []\nold-3 1707 Counter({('stored accepted', False): 1707, ('refused', True): 2}) surprises []\ncontrol-1 1187 Counter({('stored accepted', False): 196, ('refused', True): 3, ('other archive entry', False): 2}) surprises []\nlinked-1 1630 Counter({('stored accepted', False): 261, ('refused', True): 7}) surprises []\nH4 118 2026-07-15 ['', '- v8 (open; first_is_bullish) How much revenue will NVIDIA generate from stand-alone CPU sales in FY2027?: now rung 3 Neutral, judged 2026-07-15', '    Comparison point stated by that judgement: NVIDIA’s FY2027 stand-alone CPU sales forecast of $20 billion; this reference is at the lower boundary of rung 2.', \"    The system's forecast for it (our own judgement, not evidence): About $19.5 billion in FY2027: discount NVIDIA’s roughly $20 billion target because no shipment volume or deployment scale is shown, while allowing for the customer interest and favorable updated demand/access themes.\"] control (108, '2026-07-15', 'About $387B: carrying the Q1-to-Q2 sequential increase from $81.6B to the $91B Q2 guide forward gives roughly $101.5B in Q3 and $113.2B in Q4, for about $387B across FY2027.')\nH4 134 2026-07-16 ['', '- v8 (open; first_is_bullish) How much revenue will NVIDIA generate from stand-alone CPU sales in FY2027?: now rung 3 Neutral, judged 2026-07-16', \"    Comparison point stated by that judgement: NVIDIA's $20 billion FY2027 stand-alone CPU sales forecast is the market/company reference and sits at rung 2, the $20 billion lower boundary.\", \"    The system's forecast for it (our own judgement, not evidence): About $19.5 billion in FY2027: start from the $20 billion company forecast and apply a modest execution discount because the rollout and named customer interest are not accompanied by shipment volumes, deployment scale, or a sales run-rate. This is below $20 billion but above $15 billion, so it implies rung 3.\"] control (125, '2026-07-16', 'About $417 billion for FY2027. Bloomberg’s $393 billion estimate and 82% growth imply an FY2026 base of about $216 billion; Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion at 85% growth and Q2 guidance of $91 billion at 95% growth imply about $91 billion of FY2026 revenue for those quarters, leaving roughly $125 billion for the remaining quarters. Applying the guided 95% growth rate to that remainder gives approximately $81.6B + $91B + ($125B × 1.95) = $417B.')\nH4 150 2026-07-17 ['', '- v8 (open; first_is_bullish) How much revenue will NVIDIA generate from stand-alone CPU sales in FY2027?: now rung 3 Neutral, judged 2026-07-17', '    Comparison point stated by that judgement: NVIDIA’s approximately $20 billion FY2027 stand-alone CPU sales forecast is the market reference and sits at the lower boundary of rung 2.', \"    The system's forecast for it (our own judgement, not evidence): Approximately $19 billion in FY2027—an analytical estimate just below the company’s roughly $20 billion target, discounted because the evidence describes offers and customer intent but no quantified shipments or deployments.\"] control (139, '2026-07-17', 'Approximately $417 billion: FY2026 revenue was $215.9 billion; Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.6 billion at 85.2% growth implies about $44.1 billion for the prior-year quarter, and the $91 billion Q2 guide at 95% growth implies about $46.7 billion. Applying 95% growth to the remaining FY2026 revenue gives about $244 billion for FY2027 Q3–Q4, for a total near $417 billion.')\nH4 153 2026-07-18 ['', '- v8 (open; first_is_bullish) How much revenue will NVIDIA generate from stand-alone CPU sales in FY2027?: now rung 3 Neutral, judged 2026-07-17', '    Comparison point stated by that judgement: NVIDIA’s approximately $20 billion FY2027 stand-alone CPU sales forecast is the market reference and sits at the lower boundary of rung 2.', \"    The system's forecast for it (our own judgement, not evidence): Approximately $19 billion in FY2027—an analytical estimate just below the company’s roughly $20 billion target, discounted because the evidence describes offers and customer intent but no quantified shipments or deployments.\"] control (153, '2026-07-18', 'Approximately $417 billion: carrying the observed 85% Q1 growth and roughly 95% Q2 guided growth forward against FY2026 revenue of $215.9 billion implies about 90%–95% annual growth, with a central estimate near $417 billion.')\nH4 174 2026-07-20 ['', '- v8 (open; first_is_bullish) How much revenue will NVIDIA generate from stand-alone CPU sales in FY2027?: now rung 3 Neutral, judged 2026-07-20', \"    Comparison point stated by that judgement: NVIDIA's $20 billion FY2027 stand-alone CPU sales target; it sits at the lower boundary of rung 2. No separate market-consensus figure is supplied.\", \"    The system's forecast for it (our own judgement, not evidence): Approximately $19 billion in FY2027, near but below $20 billion. This discounts NVIDIA's target because shipment volume is not shown to be in hand, while the customer interest and reported cloud offering activity provide some support for approaching it.\"] control (164, '2026-07-20', 'About $417 billion for FY2027: carry the roughly 85% Q1 and 95% Q2 guided year-over-year growth run-rate forward from FY2026 revenue of $215.9 billion, with the near-term guide and demand signals supporting a high-growth outcome. This is a forecast, not a reported FY2027 result.')\nclosing ids rule 8777 Answer per the JSON schema. cites may name only the evidence ids listed above; cites_views only the dependency thesis ids listed above; theme_pushes only the theme ids listed above; a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views.\nclosing ids rule 8822 Answer per the JSON schema. cites may name only the evidence ids listed above; cites_views only the dependency thesis ids listed above; theme_pushes only the theme ids listed above; a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views.\nclosing ids rule 8848 Answer per the JSON schema. cites may name only the evidence ids listed above; cites_views only the dependency thesis ids listed above; theme_pushes only the theme ids listed above; a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views.\nclosing ids rule 8855 Answer per the JSON schema. cites may name only the evidence ids listed above; cites_views only the dependency thesis ids listed above; theme_pushes only the theme ids listed above; a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views.\nclosing ids rule 8888 Answer per the JSON schema. cites may name only the evidence ids listed above; cites_views only the dependency thesis ids listed above; theme_pushes only the theme ids listed above; a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views.\nclosing ids rule 8909 Answer per the JSON schema. cites may name only the evidence ids listed above; cites_views only the dependency thesis ids listed above; theme_pushes only the theme ids listed above; a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views.\nclosing ids rule 9021 Answer per the JSON schema. cites may name only the evidence ids listed above; cites_views only the dependency thesis ids listed above; theme_pushes only the theme ids listed above; a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md | sed -n '1,37p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PROBE-V2-RESULT.md | sed -n '12,51p'; rg -n '7,700|7700|stored v118 runs|link-pilot' docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/round37-brief.md; ls -1 poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md | sed -n '1,37p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PROBE-V2-RESULT.md | sed -n '12,51p'; rg -n '7,700|7700|stored v118 runs|link-pilot' docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/round37-brief.md; ls -1 poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# A sharpened link question, version 2 (D703; for council review before its cents probe)\n     2\t\n     3\tAlex chose to probe a sharpened wording before the paid run (D703): keep Data Center reads total revenue and the 38 negatives, remove\n     4\tunsupported links including the base effect, no blanket ban on a whole reading its part. The probe is harness-only: `window_test.py\n     5\tprobe-v2` replaces the READS and SIGN criteria texts in memory for its pass; no product file changes until a version is chosen.\n     6\t\n     7\t## 1. Prompt audit (the census's failure classes against the request sentences; AGENTS §6)\n     8\t\n     9\t| Failure class (census, `CENSUS-RESULT.md`) | The request sentence that produced it | The standard or decision on the case | Verdict |\n    10\t|---|---|---|---|\n    11\t| Part against whole, direction unsettled: v9–v14 at margins 0.03–0.09; v21–v9 flips between draws; whole-to-part and part-to-whole both occur | READS `candidate_reads_thesis`: \"a part read against its whole (...), or a quantity read against another it depends on (...)\": the second clause lets a whole \"depend on\" its part; no sentence says which reads when both fit | D537: the total carried the year's consensus and guidance that the segment's requests lacked; D260: a judgement is made against what the market expects (consensus, guidance, the stated plan) | **abstract** (two clauses, both directions, no tie-break) |\n    12\t| Across periods with an unsupported sign: v17 (FY2028 growth) reads v16 (FY2027 CPU), together, 3 of 3; v35 (FY2028 total) reads v9 (FY2027 Data Center), 1 of 3 | no READS sentence on periods (`neither` covers only \"the same quantity for the same period and scope\"); every SIGN example is within one period | the arithmetic of a growth rate (a higher base lowers next year's growth at a given level); the dependency design §2: another period of the same quantity \"may be linked\" | **missing** |\n    13\t\n    14\t## 2. The wording (changes marked; every example from another industry, none names the covered company)\n    15\t\n    16\tREADS, `candidate_reads_thesis`, appended sentence:\n    17\t> When either question could be judged with the other in view, the one whose answer the supplied text anchors less (no guidance,\n    18\t> consensus or reported figure for the quantity and full period the question asks about) is the one judged with the other's conclusion\n    19\t> in view.\n    20\t\n    21\tREADS, `neither`, appended clause (before \"sharing a company ...\"):\n    22\t> or quantities of different periods when the supplied text does not state how one period's answer moves the other's (a retailer's\n    23\t> sales this year and its sales growth next year, when the text only names both)\n    24\t\n    25\tSIGN, `opposite`, added example:\n    26\t> ...; one year's sales and the next year's sales growth at a given next-year level, since a higher base lowers the growth\n    27\t\n    28\t`thesis_reads_candidate` (\"for the same reasons with the roles swapped\") and the instructions are unchanged, so the tie-break applies\n    29\tboth ways: a part with guidance and a whole without would have the whole read the part. No direction is banned.\n    30\t\n    31\tSources (round 18 made the distinction explicit): the general tie-break and the periods clause are proposals this probe is authorized\n    32\tto test by D703, not rules already decided; D537 decided only the concrete case (Data Center revenue reading total revenue, the total\n    33\tcarrying the year's consensus), and D260 explains why guidance and consensus anchor a judgement (it governs judging, not linking). The\n    34\tbase-effect example is the arithmetic of a growth rate with the next-year level held fixed. The periods clause narrows the dependency\n    35\tdesign §2 (\"another period of the same quantity may be linked\") to \"when the supplied text states how\": a link across periods still\n    36\texists when the text gives the bridge (v35 reads v14: the FY2028 outlook translates growth into a level through the FY2027 base).\n    37\tRound 18 read the seq-148 request (dry archive, call 8744): the total carries Bloomberg's $393B FY2027 estimate, Data Center a Q1\n    12\t\n    13\t## Against the current wording (every pair proposed in some draw of either; \"3/3\" = proposed in all three draws)\n    14\t\n    15\t| pair | current wording (census) | version 2 | reading |\n    16\t|---|---|---|---|\n    17\t| v9 reads v14 | 3/3 (margins 0.05, 0.09, 0.03) | 3/3 (0.03, 0.07, 0.13) | kept; still fragile |\n    18\t| v17 (FY2028 growth) reads v16 (FY2027 CPU), together | 3/3 | 0/3 | **removed** (the base-effect risk) |\n    19\t| v35 (FY2028 total) reads v9 (FY2027 Data Center) | 1/3 | 0/3 | **removed** (no bridge) |\n    20\t| v21–v9 | 3/3, direction flips (v21 reads v9 twice, v9 reads v21 once) | v21 reads v9 2/3, never reversed | **no flip** |\n    21\t| v21 (FY2027 growth) reads v16 (FY2027 CPU) | 3/3 | 3/3 | kept |\n    22\t| v16 (total CPU) reads v14 (total revenue) | 3/3 | 3/3 | kept |\n    23\t| v2 (all credit support) reads v1 (AI-cloud credit support) | 2/3 | 0/3 | lost (defensible, round 17) |\n    24\t| v35 (FY2028 total) reads v14 (FY2027 total) | 2/3 | 0/3 | lost (defensible: the outlook bridges the base, round 18) |\n    25\t| **v14 (total revenue) reads v8 (stand-alone CPU)** | 0/3 (0.47, 0.46, 0.44: below the line) | **3/3 (0.53, 0.54, 0.58)** | **added**: a whole reading a part about 5% of it; the tie-break points the other way (the total carries the full-year estimate) |\n    26\t| v16 (total CPU) reads v8 (stand-alone CPU) | 0/3 | 1/3 | added once: a whole reading its part |\n    27\t\n    28\tProposals per draw: current wording 7, 8, 5; version 2 5, 5, 6.\n    29\t\n    30\t## What it shows\n    31\t- The periods clause did what it was written for: both unsupported links across periods are gone, and so is the defensible one\n    32\t  (v35 reads v14), whose bridge Jev did not credit.\n    33\t- The tie-break did not settle direction as written: it kept v9 reads v14 at the same thin margins, and it moved v14–v8 above the line\n    34\t  in the direction it should have refused. A whole reading a part a twentieth its size gives the total little; it also makes v14 a\n    35\t  reader, so in a paid run the total's own judgements change and the Data Center question reads a changed total.\n    36\t- Stability improved where the census flipped (v21–v9), not where it was thin (v9–v14).\n    37\t\n    38\t## Council round 20 (`codex-r20.md`): TAKE VERSION 2 TO THE PAID DESIGN, agreed\n    39\t- The PASS holds (Codex re-derived both tables, 51 jobs, the ledger and the nine store projections; no invalid draw).\n    40\t- v14 reads v8 is weak with plausible downstream harm: the total had a direct $393B FY2027 estimate and the CPU card no full-year\n    41\t  NVIDIA CPU forecast, so the tie-break favoured the CPU question reading the total; the risk is the total treating an uncertain CPU\n    42\t  forecast as incremental to an estimate that may already include it. Unmeasured: the probe bought no judgements.\n    43\t- The three sentences changed together; which sentence moved which link is unmeasured.\n    44\t- Next: version 2 as a separately versioned, reviewed product configuration, then the paid design. No third wording chosen on these\n    45\t  105 pairs (that would be selection on the probe set).\n    46\t- For the paid design: keep the whole chain (v9 reads v14, v14 reads v8); prove at $0 that the product version reproduces the probe's\n    47\t  request hashes and graph; in each paired control sample v14 and v9 fresh from their first affected judgement; per common date show\n    48\t  which CPU conclusion the linked total saw, how that total compares with its control, and which total Data Center saw; judge Data\n    49\t  Center against its own sequence's total; report days added by propagation apart; credit reconciliation only with sound arithmetic\n    50\t  and sourcing.\n4:`poc/data/link-pilot-2026-11-21/`, and the product's judging retry (`src/hivemind/views/judging.py` `round_of_judgements`,\n10:archive.sqlite, summary.json), open read-only (`file:...?mode=ro`). Do NOT open anything under `poc/data/link-pilot-2026-11-21/linked-1/`:\n27:3. Census of refused judge answers on stored v118 runs: old-1 1,610 judge calls, 1 refusal (theme ids, not evidence); old-2 1,620\nledgers\nnew-1\nnew-1.launcher.log\nnew-1.pid\nnew-2\nnew-2.launcher.log\nnew-2.pid\nnew-3\nnew-3.launcher.log\nnew-3.pid\nold-1\nold-1.launcher.log\nold-1.pid\nold-2\nold-2.launcher.log\nold-2.pid\nold-3\nold-3.launcher.log\nold-3.pid\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import collections,json,pathlib,re,sqlite3,sys\nsys.path.insert(0,'\\\\''docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window'\\\\'')\nimport contradictions\nb=pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1])\ndef op(p):\n return sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\'',uri=True)\nl=op(b/'\\\\''linked-1-copy/views.sqlite'\\\\''); c=op(b/'\\\\''control-1-copy/views.sqlite'\\\\''); old=op(pathlib.Path('\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/views.sqlite'\\\\'')); a=op(b/'\\\\''linked-1-copy/archive.sqlite'\\\\'')\nplan=json.loads(pathlib.Path('\\\\''docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/pinned-plan.json'\\\\'').read_text())\nkeys={v:(obj,meas,scope,first,last,unit) for v,obj,meas,scope,first,last,unit in l.execute('\\\\''select view_id,object_id,measure,scope,period_start,period_end,unit from views join view_keys using (view_id)'\\\\'')}\nfor draw,p in plan.items():\n print('\\\\''DRAW'\\\\'',draw, p['\\\\''graph'\\\\''])\n for v,w,*_ in p['\\\\''graph'\\\\'']:\n  print(v,keys.get(v),w,keys.get(w))\nprint('\\\\''planned Sep19 v21'\\\\'',old.execute(\\\"select count(*) from judgements where view_id='\\\\''v21'\\\\'' and publication_day='\\\\''2026-09-19'\\\\''\\\").fetchone())\nfor r in contradictions.daily(l,'\\\\''v9'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\'','\\\\''2026-07-10'\\\\'','\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\''):\n if r[1]=='\\\\''ambiguous'\\\\'':print('\\\\''AMBIG'\\\\'',r[0],r[4],r[5])\ns=json.loads((b/'\\\\''linked-1-copy/summary.json'\\\\'').read_text())\nsc=json.loads((b/'\\\\''control-1-copy/summary.json'\\\\'').read_text())\nfor ss in (s,sc):\n print(ss['\\\\''kind'\\\\''],collections.Counter((j['\\\\''view'\\\\''],j['\\\\''retry'\\\\'']) for j in ss['\\\\''judge attempts at the transport'\\\\'']))\nprint('\\\\''No exact reference to a dependency in accepted DC forecast, review list:'\\\\'')\nr=l.execute(\\\"select judgement_id,publication_day,implied_outcome,reasons from judgements where view_id='\\\\''v9'\\\\'' and publication_day>='\\\\''2026-07-10'\\\\'' order by publication_day\\\").fetchall()\nfor id,day,f,remarks in r:\n if not re.search(r'\\\\''\\\\b(?:dependenc\\\\w*|v14|share|mix)\\\\b|\\\\b9[0-3](?:[.][0-9]+)?%'\\\\'',f,re.I): print(id,day,f,remarks[-350:])\nprint('\\\\''reader places in v9'\\\\'',len(r))\n' '/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
