{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"agent_message","text":"**Agreed on A. Pair 1 is inconclusive because the control double-refused. Close this comparison without a redraw or a resume.** Linked-1 completed all 82 days, passed every run check, and committed the four links you listed. Total spend was **$1.70 of $2.50**. The registered verdict stops at the invalid control, before the forecast and harm readings can decide the pilot. [Linked summary](/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/linked-1-copy/summary.json) · [Verdict order](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:136)\n\n### What to report beside the verdict\n\n- **Refusals crossed the harm threshold on the completed overlap.** On 200 matched question-days, I reproduced **5 linked refusals versus 1 control refusal**, exactly the four-extra threshold. Two linked refusals were outside that overlap. A successful control resume would bring both September 8 refusals into the count. The pinned schedule would also bring in the linked September 19 refusal if the control completed that judgement. Those changes alone reduce the excess to two or three. That is a concrete reason C cannot stand as the registered reading. [Matched-day counting code](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/verdict.py:225)\n\n- **The part used the whole as a useful check in this draw.** The parser flagged 3 of 60 shared dates in linked-1 and 28 of 60 in control-1. I read all 12 linked dates the parser marked definite, overlapping or ambiguous across the full window. None showed Data Center above total revenue. The five sampled control contradictions were real. On July 22, for example, linked Data Center forecast **$352B** from a **$387.3B** company total. The parser picked up the company figure as the segment forecast. I’d report that the link kept the forecasts consistent in the readings checked. “Removed the contradiction class” goes beyond this one draw and this sampling. [Linked judgements](/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/linked-1-copy/views.sqlite) · [Parser](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/contradictions.py:50)\n\n- **The reverse link produced four CPU double counts.** I shuffled all 71 answers, hid their dates and IDs, and marked four before restoring them. Your list was already in the brief, so this is an exploratory second read. My list matched yours: **July 15 (118), July 16 (134), July 17 (150), and July 18 (153)**. Each added $19–19.5B to a roughly $387B company-wide forecast without showing that the baseline excluded CPU sales. All four crossed $400B because of that addition, and the last held through July 19. July 20 reversed it. The “63 omit CPU” count applies to the forecast field alone. Across forecasts and reasons, **only three omit CPU or v8**. Any one confirmed double count would have stopped a valid pilot under H4. [Linked archive](/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/linked-1-copy/archive.sqlite) · [H4 rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:129)\n\n- **Six of the seven fresh linked refusals mixed up which list an ID belonged in.** Two put the dependency `v14` in evidence **citations**, and neither put it in an evidence push. Four put theme IDs in dependency citations alongside a valid dependency. The seventh used an unlisted evidence tag. All seven passed on retry. The system prompt’s theme sentence omits `cites_views`, but the **actual requests explicitly forbid theme IDs there** in the closing instruction. The answer format still accepts arbitrary strings in those fields. Across the three named historical runs and the fresh calls in both pilot arms, I verified **17 membership refusals in 5,408 distinct archived attempts**. All 5,389 committed answers fit the proposed lists. I could not reproduce the roughly 7,700 denominator from the named copies. [Answer format](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:55) · [Closing request instruction](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:180)\n\n### One recommendation for Alex\n\n**Open a citation-only judge version and run one $0 test of the exact lists, from request generation through answer checking.** Prove that the stored accepted answers still fit, the observed bad tags are excluded, and a field with zero allowed IDs accepts only an empty list. This proves which tags the format permits. Whether the model reliably picks the right source remains a separate measurement.\n\nKeep the direction change separate. Code can enforce a direction policy once the accounting relationship is established. Today the keys label the failing stand-alone CPU question as `other`, so the proposed component-revenue rule would **miss the bad link in all three probe draws**. And choosing whether a component forecast can inform the total is a judgement call. A retailer with separate, non-overlapping store and online forecasts can legitimately build its total from those parts. The prior design explicitly allowed that direction. [Pinned graphs](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/pinned-plan.json) · [Prior direction rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md:14)\n\nUsing the new judge in both arms would be fair for a **new test of what links add to that judge**. The original question was whether the linked product should replace frozen v118. That comparison would still be open. I also verified that changing only the allowed citation list changes the archive lookup key for a non-reader request. The current runner would refuse that miss, so the roughly $2 estimate needs a new replay proof before it can support a send. [Comparison objective](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:10) · [Runner admission rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/paid_run.py:172)"}}
